* soft-start-loop-gain -- klt sim circuit body template, margin deck (issue #451).
*
* tb_ss_loop_gain.spice.in's circuit, in the shape `klt sim` accepts: no
* .control block, no model .lib cards, no .temp (klt binds all of those per
* corner). The deck's single .control block sweeps ramp state x C_eff x ESR with
* `alter` and chains op / ac / alter / ac per point; here the Tian dual
* injection is `analysis.passes` (see klt_run.py), C_eff / ESR / the load model
* are baked into the body, and BOTH the supply and the ramp state are `.param`
* axes of the request (`corners.params`, alterparam + reset), not `alter` of a
* source. loop-stability/testbench/klt_body.spice.in measured `alter vin`
* moving the crossover ~3 % against the deck; the same reasoning applies to
* `alter Vssr`, so Vssr is driven by `.param vssr`, never altered.
*
* Tokens (klt_run.py substitutes the at-sign-delimited names used in the cards
* below; they are not spelled out in this header because a substitution here
* would land in a comment):
*
*   ILOAD, RLOAD   the phase's load model (ideal sink XOR 36 ohm, the other
*                  parked at 0 A / 1e12 ohm), as the deck has it
*   CEFF, ESR      the swept output network
*   SSR_SOURCE     `Vssr SSRPIN 0 DC {vssr}` for a pinned phase, or a comment
*                  for `anchor` (SSRPIN left unconnected)
*   DC_SEED        empty, or sweep.py's dc_seed_lines() for a retry
*
* The DUT netlist is the SSR-instrumented ldo_core_<variant>.spice that
* sweep.py already builds; klt_batch.stage() copies it to dut.spice.

.include "dut.spice"

Vin VIN 0 DC {vsup}
Ven EN 0 DC {vsup}
Vref VREF 0 DC 1.2
.param vsup=3.3
.param vssr=0

* Port order: VIN VOUT EN VSS ERRAMP_OUT PASS_GATE VREF SSR
Xdut VIN VOUT EN 0 AINJ BINJ VREF SSRPIN ldo_core

@SSR_SOURCE@

* Tian dual-injection network; both AC magnitudes are 0 here, the passes set them.
Vinj AINJ BINJ DC 0 AC 0
Iinj 0 BINJ DC 0 AC 0

Iload VOUT 0 DC @ILOAD@
Rload VOUT NLD @RLOAD@
Vlmeas NLD 0 DC 0
Resr VOUT NESR @ESR@
Cout NESR 0 @CEFF@

.model dclamp d(is=1e-14 cjo=0 tt=0 n=1 rs=0)
Dclamp 0 VOUT dclamp

@DC_SEED@
